# The markdown identity corpus is byte-exact by definition: these fixtures
# exist to assert that the editor gives back the bytes it was given, so git
# must not touch their line endings, whitespace or encoding on the way in or
# out. Without this, a checkout on a machine with core.autocrlf=true would
# rewrite the fixtures and the test would assert the wrong thing (or pass for
# the wrong reason).
# ``-text`` stops the EOL conversion; a bare ``diff`` puts the textual diff
# back, which ``-text`` would otherwise turn off (a reviewer would see
# "Binary files differ" instead of the fixture).
web/test/markdown-corpus/** -text diff
